    "created_at": "2016-04-06T20:26:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-06T20:26:06Z",
    "body": "> @kitcambridge I think we should do both. We'd say that if the user agent has dismissal UI and the user dismisses, the answer is \"default\".\n\nThat prevents UI like Firefox's where the user can re-open the prompt and make an explicit decision later. It seems like the callback should be un-deprecated and Firefox's UI should be allowed.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
